Jack had heard about the fabled Amulet of Yendor.  Never being one to pass
up a challenge, he donned his fedora, grabbed his trusty bullwhip, sack, 
tinning kit, magic marker (!), and pick axe, and headed for the dungeon.

Well, down on the first level, Jack only had a little trouble.  He encountered
his first cave spider, whipped it, and ate its meat.  He felt healthier for
the experience. (!)  Mosying along the corridors, Jack happened upon a
blindfold along the way.  He grabbed it.  "Who knows, it may come in
handy..."  Jack also found a tin of spinach just lying around. (!)  Jack has
always loved spinach.  Jack ate lunch.  He even had one other food ration
to spare.

Jack and his faithful dog Ripper went down a stair case...  There, Jack
discovered a chain mail lying around.  Ripper seemed to like it, so
Jack tried it on, and continued his quest.

Jack was searching the walls of a room when a hideous half-man, half-rat
happened upon him.  Jack had encountered these things before, and ran for
a corner, where he only had to defend himself on three sides.  (In case
it summoned its foul bretheren.)  It did exactly that.  The room was
crawling with the disgusting rodents.  The rat-were sank a nasty byte into
Jack, and Jack felt feaverish.  (Not to mention that Jack could only
stand another round like this!)  "God help me."  He muttered.  And Lo!
A golden glow surrounded him, he felt much better, and he felt purified!
Phew! >Snap< >Crunch< >Ouch!<  "That damn rat-were bit me again!"

Jack, near death, scrawled "Elbereth" on the ground, and stood still like
a statue.  Jack transformed into a rat, (the transformation wipping out
the scrawl), and was beseiged by the rodents.  RatJack tried to attack,
but couldn't budge under the weight of every thing he was carrying.
RatJack decided to turn the tables, and summoned a few bretheren of his own.
The ploy worked!

The room was filled with warring rodents: clawing, snapping, and biting
each other.  RatJack dropped everything, squirmed free of his pack, and
ran for the down stairs, a few feet away...

"Phew, free!  Well. (Geeze, I sure am hungry.)  What's in this new room?"
RatJack proceded to search all the walls of the barren room with the
up-stairs case in the middle.  It had one door, but it was locked, and
RatJack hadn't any means of opening it.  (Rats don't exactly kick doors
open, ya know.)  "Man, I'm starving... And I had to leave all my loot
upstairs."  "God, please, I'm very weak, help me out this once more..."
Jack had a bad feeling about this.

RatJack, left to no other recourse, set to go upstairs, and feast upon
his bretheren.  "Mmmph, urg..  Geeze, how did I get down these things?"
RatJack couldn't climb the stairs in such a weakened state.

Hours later, a Kobold shaman must have opened the door to the room in which
RatJack died, only to find the corpse of a frenzied, frantic, frustrated,
rat who scurried himself to death in little circles all alone in a locked
room...

